<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 2.908 µm in Drosophila buzzatii (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 82.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements the Schnakenberg PDE and the closed-form wavenumber, renders a 12-frame growth GIF at 720×540, and orders buzzatii (2.908 µm, 584 modes) against bipectinata (85.92 µm, 19 modes) and cyrtoloma (207.6 µm, 8 modes) at 0 Ma. Morphometric credit is partial until the KS, segmentation, and ablation panel are re-scored. Overall 82.9/100 (faithfulness 81.6, reproducibility 86.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 00782eec; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 00782eec, image/png, 469642 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6 (sha256 e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6), spec_fingerprint 08fa3b6fbda37d14034e66aaa32be6a4f2884d2974f79734f2b5414d7f6640c2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 08fa3b6fbda37d14034e66aaa32be6a4f2884d2974f79734f2b5414d7f6640c2; artifact_sha256: e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=61a3792c4a139711..., datasets/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=21d216f74bbb2735...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous field can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Norry, Vilardi & Hasson 1997: inversion-sensitive correlations among size traits in D. buzzatii.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so lambda_c = 2.908 um on this Jacobian, with D_v/D_u = 29. | Discrete-mode lambda across 14 gamma scales is correlated with the closed form.; transfer_boundary: Norry's wing/thorax allometry is used only as the statement that organ length changes mode count N = L/lambda, not lambda itself.; does_not_claim: That Norry measured a 2.9 µm pigment wavelength. | That the species card is a wing micrograph.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Put the two-sample KS distance between the species-card radial spectrum and the pure Schnakenberg field into the measurement sidecar (value must differ from 0).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Segment the canonical card and report foreground fraction, circularity, and structure-tensor coherency against a reference that is not the measured value.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Show the equal-diffusion ablation on the comparison figure, not only inside --self-test.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Report the saturated-field wavelength separately from the linear 2.908 µm target so the coarsening offset is a measured residual, not a hidden mismatch.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.29e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

